\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar broadly depressed, yen hostage of BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2002\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 4 (Reuters) - The dollar was squeezed to fresh multi-month lows against the euro and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia on Tuesday after another fall in U.S. share prices fuelled worries about a decline in fund flows into dollar assets. \par \par \uc2  Only against the yen did the greenback manage to hold its own as threats of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities kept dealers wary of unloading the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Despite recent robust economic data, U.S. shares have failed to climb - most recently on mistrust of the accounting practices of corporate America. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones industrial average fell 2.17 percent, its biggest one-day percentage decline in four months. \par \par \uc2  The Dow is now at its lowest level in eight months. \par \par \uc2  The abrupt resignation of the chairman of conglomerate Tyco International Ltd and news that the treasurer of energy company El Paso Corp had died in an apparent suicide hurt already-nervous sentiment for U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. seems to have suffered a compound fracture," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that investors will continue to flee from the U.S. share market pushed up the euro to a fresh 16-month high of 94.25 cents from around 94.05/10 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders said the euro could soon test its 17-month high of 95.95 set in January 2001 given the hands-off approach of euro zone officials. \par \par \uc2  The current chairman of the euro zone finance ministers' group, Rodrigo Rato, said on Monday there was a broad consensus that the momentum of economic recovery in the euro region was building, mainly due to external demand. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the Europe's common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slightly firmer at 116.39 yen, up nearly a half yen from the same time on Monday. \par \par \uc2  BOJ THREATS DOMINATE \par \par \uc2  The dollar was little changed against the yen, held hostage by threats of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market three times last month in a bid to stem the yen's rise, which is seen as a threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tentative export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday in particular took many dealers by a surprise because of its unusual timing - after three p.m. local time (0600 GMT) when dealers are starting to close their books before the weekend. \par \par \uc2  "Few people thought they would start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after three p.m. on Friday. That has made us think the BOJ could come any minute," said the Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa repeated on Tuesday that recent trading in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had been volatile and that the authorities were monitoring the market. \par \par \uc2  Similar comments have preceded \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was pinned down near 123.53/58 yen, little changed from its late U.S. levels. \par \par \uc2  Trade was range-bound partly because some Japanese dealers were distracted by the World Cup soccer finals, some dealers said. Japan, which is co-hosting the event with South Korea, plays Belgium in its opener from 0900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR UNDER PRESSURE \par \par \uc2  The dollar slipped to around 1.5584 Swiss francs, within a hair of the recent low of 1.5578, a break of which would take the greenback to its lowest level since January 2000. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also weak against Canadian dollar, which has weathered concerns about the political fallout from the sudden sacking late on Sunday of Paul Martin as finance minister. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was trading around C$1.5252 per U.S. dollar, or 65.56 cents - its highest level since last August and the peak from which it began its slide to record lows. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the Canadian dollar hit a low of C$1.5420 to the dollar, or 64.85 cents. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar also hit its highest level since September 2000 near 57.60 U.S. cents, more than one percent above its level at the start of the week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0554 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   03 Jun. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9421   0.9408   +0.14    +5.81   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen        123.60   123.56   +0.03    -6.10   131.63\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    116.40   116.32   +0.07    -0.72   117.24\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.5592   1.5639   -0.30    -6.04   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr        1.4633   1.4632   +0.01    +0.63   1.4541\par  Can/dlr        1.5250   1.5269   -0.12    -4.19   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr        0.5753   0.5711   +0.74   +12.67   0.5106\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss  1.4685   1.4675   +0.07    -0.64   1.4780\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg    0.6433   0.6431   +0.03    +5.06   0.6123\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...  Debt... Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f