\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Dlr-Buying Lifts Tsys, Helping US Fund Its Curr Acc \b0\par\par\uc2  By Grainne McCarthy \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 1,286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2002\par 17:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Underscoring its determination not to let a strong yen derail the world's second largest economy's fragile cyclical recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Tuesday, fleetingly pushing the dollar over a yen higher. \par \par \uc2  Indirectly, they are also helping out U.S. authorities, who are otherwise reluctant to join the Japanese in their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign. \par \par \uc2  Estimates based on the latest round of dollar purchases bring to over $20 billion the amount that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  - acting via the Bank of Japan - has forked out over the past couple of weeks. That's a phenomenon that's having a substantial impact on U.S. Treasurys, as the BOJ uses the extra dollars acquired to buy U.S. securities. \par \par \uc2  In a somewhat ironic twist, the BOJ is thus giving a helping hand in keeping U.S. interest rates low, which some analysts reckon might even overshadow any Bush administration opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy tool. \par \par \uc2  "There can be no complaints from the U.S. here," said Alan Ruskin, research director at 4Cast financial consultancy in New York. "The BOJ may be working alone and perhaps even against the U.S. Treasury's philosophy of respecting market forces in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but slowing the dollar's decline and delivering lower U.S. rates at the margin all benefits the wider interests of the U.S. " \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's apparent substantial Treasury purchases also come amid signs that foreign investors might be ending their love affair with dollar-denominated assets, which has helped sustain the amazing resilience of the dollar over the past seven years while cheaply financing the deficit in the current account. In reinvesting their newly-acquired dollars in the U.S., the BOJ is helping to smooth out some otherwise negative trends in portfolio flows, in turn helping to offset the chances of any sort of collapse in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "For those who are looking for a soft-landing, there are probably few better quarters to seek comfort than in the hands of the BOJ that it's apt to fight any sharp dollar slide tooth and nail," said Ruskin. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, many market watchers reckon the BOJ has embarked on what could be a lengthy period of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation. For one, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which naturally places hardly any limits on how much it might ultimately pump into the market. \par \par \uc2  The fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being executed mostly via \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  desks at Tokyo banks - and not via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or Federal Reserve - is also firming speculation that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decided to go it alone with in its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  endeavors and might be willing to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for as long as it takes to draw some sort of dollar support line in the sand. \par \par \uc2  So far, it doesn't seem to have achieved that aim. With each bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar has generally enjoyed a knee-jerk injection of support - usually jumping about a full yen - but has then almost always slipped back relatively quickly. \par \par \uc2  The reaction on Tuesday was true to this trend. Traders reckon the BOJ spent anywhere between $1 billion and $5 billion, taking advantage of thin \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market conditions, with London closed for the Queen's Jubilee holiday and stepping into the market after the close of trade in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately propelled the dollar about a yen higher, but the greenback quickly began to slip again, falling below the Y124 threshold and keeping the risk of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  very high in traders' minds. \par \par \uc2  Part of the reason the BOJ and finance ministry aren't reaping obvious success, analysts think, is due to the very fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is acting alone. In not going through the usual channels at the ECB or the Fed, the BOJ is arguably getting a bit less bang for its buck, with many traders quick to dismiss the longer term effectiveness of Japan's independent efforts to run against a broad tide of bearish dollar sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, in contrast to some of the previous rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - where the BOJ was apparently acting to temper what appeared to be independent yen strength - this time its dollar purchases came at a time when the greenback is broadly weak. "`We are seeing dollar weakness across the board and the BOJ is endeavoring to swim against it," said Rebecca Patterson, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with JP Morgan in NY. \par \par \uc2  What's more, in conducting the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  via Tokyo banks and not always immediately following up its purchases with an official confirmation, Japan is also diluting the effects to a certain extent. Some analysts believe this shows the MOF is trying to be less predictable with its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation efforts - but it also runs the risk of appearing erratic and inconsistent, which in turn could naturally limit the success of its overall goal. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par        Some Glimmers Of Success\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On some other levels however, Japan's efforts are reaping some fruit.\par "The question is where would the exchange rate be now, if they hadn't\par been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Ruskin, at 4Cast. "If they're trying to place\par some speed bumps on the yen's rise, then they've achieved that. If\par they're trying to turn it around, they've failed."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In using the bulk of the proceeds to purchase Treasurys, Japan's\par monetary authorities are also indirectly reviving a debate as to how the\par BOJ buying foreign bonds might help to weaken the yen, while at the same\par time support U.S. interest rates. That idea, which sparked fevered\par market speculation late last year, also fed talk that the U.S. was ready\par to tolerate a weaker yen in exchange for Japanese buying of U.S. bonds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Many analysts rubbished the idea back then, largely because of the\par fact that it would have resulted in simply running Japan's presses to\par print massive amounts of yen. But, according to fixed income market\par watchers, that is exactly what the BOJ appears to be doing now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some of the buying interest in Treasury bills so far Tuesday in New\par York may be attributable to the MO. acting via the BOJ, said Gerry\par Lucas, senior government strategist at Merrill Lynch in New York.\par Although \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trades take two days to settle - which means\par any MO. money at play at the short end of the Treasury market might stem\par from last week's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - "that doesn't mean they can't buy it\par forward," so the effects could be more immediate,  Lucas said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last week's auction of two-year Treasury notes was well bid, which\par "makes it highly probable that the BOJ acting on behalf of the MO. was a\par participant," Lucas said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other informed market watchers suggest the BOJ really has no\par alternative other than to use the dollars to buy U.S. bonds, given the\par lack of appeal in bringing the funds home where near-zero interest rates\par render Japanese bonds relatively unattractive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par More definitive clues about the extent of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par Treasury bonds and bills purchases may come in the latest custody\par holdings data, which the Federal Reserve will release on Thursday. The\par Fed acts as a custodian in accounts it maintains on behalf of foreign\par official institutions, including central banks. Last Thursday this\par showed the institution's holdings of securities for foreign central\par banks shot up $8.7 billion for the week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Grain McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4156;\par grainne.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (John Parry contributed to this report)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020604dy64006mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
