\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF Kuroda: "Unnatural" For Yen To Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2002\par 02:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remains unchanged in the face of the surging yen, a top Japanese finance official said Friday, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be preparing for a new round of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "As I've said before, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is absolutely unchanged," Vice Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said when asked about the potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Kuroda added that it is unnatural for the yen to strengthen against the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market twice last week after the dollar fell below the key Y124 barrier. A strong yen, the authorities fear, could foil Japan's nascent economic turnaround by driving up the cost of exports. \par \par \uc2  In New York trading Thursday the dollar plunged to a six month low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to Y122.86, before rebounding slightly to the low Y123 range. \par \par \uc2  Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most notably the euro, hit multi-month highs against the dollar Thursday, but Kuroda said the yen deserved an exemption from recent anti-dollar trends. \par \par \uc2  "The Euro has been undervalued until now, so the fact that it would strengthen (against the dollar) is understandable," he said. "But Japan's case is different." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda did not elaborate on his statement, but the government has consistently said that exchange rates should reflect economic fundamentals, a stance Kuroda repeated at a meeting with European finance officials Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's recent weakness across the board has been driven by skepticism about a rebound in U.S. corporate earnings, as well as questions about how the U.S. will continue to finance the twin gaps in its current account and federal budget deficits. \par \par \uc2  Amid growing global bearishness on the dollar, some doubt the effectiveness of further yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities, particularly as the small gains made by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen after last week's moves have already been erased. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of 0205 GMT the dollar was trading at Y123.32.\par      -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par jonathan.soble@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020531dy5v0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
