\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar solidly higher on data,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2002\par 21:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1930 GMT - The dollar remained on firm ground in late New York trade after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying dollars for yen in the late Tokyo/early European and New York trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  - Surprisingly strong U.S. regional manufacturing data for May; better than expected April U.S. factory orders data; and higher than expected May consumer sentiment, as measured by the University of Michigan all contributed to dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. The yen's recent and fast rising strength against the dollar as investors take a shine to Japanese assets threatened to choke off growth in the important export sector of the economy, prompting the authorities to step in and try to slow the move. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar/yen trades at 124.31 yen , up 0.87 percent compared with Thursday's New York close. However, the yen failed to reach the overnight high of 124.59 yen. \par \par \uc2  - Jiji press earlier reported the BOJ stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the dollar was trading around 123.60-70 yen, spending less than $3 billion. \par \par \uc2  - The New York Federal Reserve says it would not comment on whether or not the bank participated in any market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while several sources said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred through the use of dealer banks' night desks in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  - Euro/dollar fell to a session low of of 92.82 cents , before climbing back to 93.16 cents, still a loss of 0.72 percent on the day and one full cent below Thursday's 15-month high. \par \par \uc2  - Euro/yen gains are pared back, trading at 115.82 yen , off 0.11 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar/Swiss franc surges to 1.5735 francs , a gain of 0.74 percent on the day, and off the 2-1/2 year low reached on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  - Sterling/dollar falls to $1.4547, down 0.72 percent on the day. Euro/sterling rises to 63.98 pence, up 0.13 percent on the day, but below Thursday's 15-1/2 month high. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar's weak spot against commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains intact. Australian dollar/U.S. dollar trades at 56.69 cents, a gain of 0.66 percent, but off the earlier 16-month high of 56.96 cents. U.S. dollar/Canadian dollar falls to 9-1/2 month low of C$1.5263. \par \par \uc2  -. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020531dy5v0116z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
