\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar rebounds to session highs vs yen and euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2002\par 19:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1732 GMT - Dollar moves toward session highs against the yen and the euro on surprisingly strong U.S. economic data as well as repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and choke off its export-damaging effects. \par \par \uc2  - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed to Reuters on Friday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during New York trading time to prevent the yen from rising further. Earlier, Japanese authorities confirmed they had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen during late Tokyo/early European trading hours. Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  marks the third day in the last two weeks that Japan has stepped into the market to stem the yen's advance against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar/yen trades at 124.31 yen , up 0.87 percent compared with Thursday's New York close. However, the yen failed to reach the overnight high of 124.59 yen. \par \par \uc2  - Jiji press earlier reported the BOJ stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the dollar was trading around 123.60-70 yen, spending less than $3 billion. \par \par \uc2  - The New York Federal Reserve says it would not comment on whether or not the bank participated in any market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while several sources said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred through the use of dealer banks' night desks in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  - Euro/dollar danced near fresh session low of of 92.82 cents, before climbing back to 93 cents, still a loss of 0.72 percent on the day. On Thursday the euro hit a 15-month high of 94.16 cents. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers cite the dollar's broad-based rally on the back of surprisingly stronger than expected May regional manufacturing and April factory order data. \par \par \uc2  - Euro/yen gains are pared back, trading at 115.73 yen , off 0.11 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar/Swiss franc surges to 1.5741 francs , a gain of 0.78 percent on the day, and off the 2-1/2 year low reached on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020531dy5v00y42\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
