\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar bolstered by  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  yen-selling  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2002\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 31 (Reuters) - The dollar leapt against the yen as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, fearing its recent strength would damage the nation's tentative export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  The greenback - which sank to six-month lows below 123 yen on Thursday - shot up more than one percent to around 124.60 after the first action in late Asian trade, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's third day of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in less than two weeks. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in early European trade and also half way through the European morning, and dealers estimate it bought around $5-6 billion in total on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "They have a higher amount of appetite for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and they do repeated rounds. It does provide fear that any yen strength will be met by more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Michael Lewis, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  "The size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have increased since last week (but) the power of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is short lived and underlying pressure on the yen is still there." \par \par \uc2  Banking sources estimate the BOJ bought $8.56 billion for yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two days of action last week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has fallen over seven percent both against the euro and the yen in the last fortnight as doubts over the pace of the U.S. recovery have dimmed the once unrivalled appeal of U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was struggling to hold its post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains on offers from Japanese exporters and had fallen back below 124 yen by 1211 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "(Japanese authorities) can continue to play the market but the political environment won't support it. What they can do is to slow the (yen's) ascent," said Stacey Seltzer, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Brown Brothers Harriman. \par \par \uc2  The greenback was also trading within sight of the previous session's 15-month lows beyond $0.94 against the euro and 28-month lows against the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said London trading activity was likely to decrease in the course of the day as the first World Cup soccer match got underway and the city wound down for a four-day holiday weekend. \par \par \uc2  WEATHERS DOWNGRADE \par \par \uc2  The euro also vaulted one percent to 116.65 yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - its highest level in two weeks - before drifting back to 116.20. \par \par \uc2  Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen was holding firm, taking a two-notch downgrade of Japan's sovereign rating by Moody's Investors Service in its stride. \par \par \uc2  Moody's cut its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating on Japanese government debt by two notches to A2, putting Japan far behind all other major industrialised countries. \par \par \uc2  The dollar initially rose a little after the announcement, but soon shed its gains. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the impact was muted not only because it had been widely expected but also because the outlook on the new rating was stable, suggesting no further cuts for some time. \par \par \uc2  Vincent Truglia, a managing director at Moody's, told Reuters there was less than a 50 percent chance that Japan's rating would go on review again in the next 12 to 24 months. \par \par \uc2  US CONCERNS DOMINANT \par \par \uc2  The Wall Street Journal online edition on Friday quoted U.S. President George W. Bush's chief economic advisor Lawrence Lindsey as saying the U.S. still favours a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and playing down the latest drop in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market is now more dominated by worries about the U.S. economy rather than Japan, and that the dollar's near-term outlook was bleak. \par \par \uc2  U.S. data including factory orders, the University of Michigan sentiment survey and the Chicago Purchasing Managers' Index are all due later in the day and will be closely watched for clues on the strength of the U.S. recovery. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were casting a wary eye on U.S. stocks, which have shown persistent weakness in recent weeks due to worries about corporate profits and accounting practices. On Friday U.S. stock futures were pointing to a firmer opening on Wall Street, giving some relief to dollar bulls. \par \par \uc2  The market has U.S. ISM purchasing managers' data for May, U.S. jobs data, Japanese gross domestic product for the first quarter and a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meeting next week. \par \par \uc2  "Next week will be a big data week and key for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Anticipation of soft data means there is a possibility the market could push the dollar yet lower, at least against the euro," Seltzer said. \par \par \uc2  An early estimate of euro zone consumer prices data showed inflation running at 2.0 percent on the year in May compared with 2.4 in April, falling to match the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target ceiling of two percent for the first time this year. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone M3 money supply data showed a surprising rise to 7.5 percent in April from 7.3 previously but analysts said they expected it to have little immediate impact on interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020531dy5v00ojo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
