\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar, euro jump after  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 820 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2002\par 10:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 31 (Reuters) - The dollar jumped against the yen late Friday afternoon in Asian trade as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fearing its recent rise would dent the nation's export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen was firm near its six-month high against the dollar recorded the previous day, braving a bigger-than-expected downgrade of Japan's sovereign rating by Moody's Investors Service. \par \par \uc2  The dollar shot up to 124.60 yen from around 123.10 yen after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third time this month. \par \par \uc2  "I think the market had expected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It shows the determination of the authorities not to allow rapid moves," said a European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The euro also vaulted to 116.65 yen - its highest level in two weeks - from around 115.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the yen was holding firm, taking Moody's downgrade of Japanese government debt in its stride. \par \par \uc2  A little after noon in Tokyo (0300 GMT), Moody's Investors Service said it cut its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating on Japanese government debt by two notches to A2 from Aa3, putting Japan far behind all other major industrialised countries, which have a rating of triple A or double A at worst. \par \par \uc2  The decision was within but at the largest end of market expectations, as Moody's had said in the past the results of its review on Japan could be between no change to a two-notch downgrade. \par \par \uc2  The dollar initially rose a little after the announcement, to 123.40/50 yen from 123.25 yen. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback soon lost its momentum and slid to around 123.00 yen, below its late U.S. levels around 123.25 and just shy of its six-month low of 122.82. \par \par \uc2  "The Moody's impact was as short-lived as a firework," said Toshiyuki Aoyagi, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nissho Iwai Financial Link. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen was supported not only because the downgrade had long been expected but also because the rating firm placed its rating outlook on Japan at stable, suggesting there will be no more rate cuts on Japan for some time. \par \par \uc2  Vincent Truglia, a managing director at Moody's, told Reuters there was less than a 50 percent chance that Japan's rating would go on review again in the next 12 to 24 months. \par \par \uc2  US CONCERNS DOMINANT \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market is now more dominated by worries about the U.S. economy rather than Japan, and that the dollar's near-term outlook was bleak. The dollar fell nearly eight percent both against the euro and the yen in the last two months. \par \par \uc2  With concerns over the pace of a U.S. recovery, its current account deficit, and to top it all off a poor performance on Wall Street, the euro rose to 93.98/03 cents in late afternoon, up from 93.70 in late U.S. trade, closing in on its 16-month peak of 94.15 recorded the previous day. \par \par \uc2  It backed off slightly to 93.75 after the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which dealers said was in dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  A series of economic indicators released this morning was in line with market forecasts and with views that the Japanese economy is heading towards a cyclical recovery. \par \par \uc2  Average spending of wage earners rose a real 0.9 percent in April from a year earlier. The ratio of job offers to applicants rose to slightly to 0.52. \par \par \uc2  "The rise of the job-offers-to-applicants ratio is kind of encouraging news. It is a typical coincident indicator and moves in line with the recovery of industrial production," said Takehiro Sato, an economist at Morgan Stanley. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0622 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   30 May. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9375   0.9367   +0.09    +5.29   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen        124.06   123.24   +0.67    -5.75   131.63\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    116.36   115.53   +0.72    -0.75   117.24\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.5596   1.5619   -0.15    -6.01   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr        1.4652   1.4653   -0.01    +0.76   1.4541\par  Can/dlr        1.5342   1.5338   +0.03    -3.61   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr        0.5672   0.5632   +0.71   +11.08   0.5106\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss  1.4624   1.4633   -0.06    -1.06   1.4780\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg    0.6395   0.6390   +0.08    +4.44   0.6123\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...  Debt... Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par