\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 4- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to stem yen gains. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2002\par 21:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yen for dollars repeatedly on Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during Asian, European and U.S. trade in an increasingly aggressive effort to keep the surging yen from derailing Japan's export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  Friday marks the third time in just over a week that Japanese officials have stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  After a downgrade of Japan's sovereign rating failed to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japanese authorities spent what market sources estimated was well over one trillion yen ($8.0 billion) to buy dollars and thus rein in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which continued its upward charge despite the rating action. \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service, in a closely watched decision, delivered a bigger-than-expected two-notch cut to Japan's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating on government debt to A2 from Aa3 on Friday. It changed the outlook to stable. \par \par \uc2  Japan's growing concern about the yen's recent rally was apparent in the MOF's decision to step into \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets during U.S. trading, after having already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Asian and European trade. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was estimated to have bought $8.56 billion for yen last week, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday and Thursday to cap the yen's strength against the dollar, banking sources said. \par \par \uc2  Data released by the BOJ showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  paid 1.067 trillion yen ($8.64 billion) to the private sector in May through its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which mostly represents \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Because \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions are settled two business days after deals are done, the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday will be settled next month and is not reflected in the BOJ data on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Following last week's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ministry again on Friday bought dollars for yen as the greenback fell to around 123.00 yen, within striking distance of a six-month low of 122.82 hit on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements were too rapid. We will continue to monitor the market and take appropriate action as needed," Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the Finance Ministry's international bureau, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "We will act whenever the timing is most effective." \par \par \uc2  His boss, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, issued a similar comment in a statement prepared for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Neither the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  nor the New York Federal Reserve Bank commented on whether they participated in the yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar initially jumped to 124.45/50 yen compared with 123.10/20 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market dealers said. Subsequent waves of Japanese dollar-buying in European and U.S. trading hours failed to lift the dollar above overnight peaks at 124.59 yen and by 2:44 p.m. (1844 GMT), the greenback had eased back to 124.25 yen . \par \par \uc2  IT'S NOT OVER YET \par \par \uc2  "I think they will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more in the future since if left untouched, the dollar would continue to slip against the yen," said Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "They will have to continue ... and a fairly big amount of funds will be needed for this," he said, referring to the MOF's pain threshold of 124 yen. \par \par \uc2  It was the third time since last week that the Bank of Japan had come into the market on behalf of the MOF, which has said it was acting to prevent rapid fluctuations in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  Japan is seen worried about a strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dimming export competitiveness and eating away at the profits of exporting companies. \par \par \uc2  The latest string of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  started on May 22 after the yen climbed to a five-month high of 123.50 yen to the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again the following day, pushing the dollar up almost one full yen to around 124.80. \par \par \uc2  The yen has been strong in recent weeks because of growing evidence that Japan has pulled out of its third recession in a decade. \par \par \uc2  Economists expect growth in Japan in the first quarter could have reached an annualized rate of more than eight percent, handily outpacing the United States. The figure will be announced on Friday, June 7. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020531dy5v00fwb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
