\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar bogged down in Tokyo, wary of BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 869 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2002\par 05:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 31 (Reuters) - The dollar failed to set a clear direction versus the euro and the yen by late morning on Friday, with traders trapped by fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a weak Wall Street and uncertainty over the U.S. recovery. \par \par \uc2  The market was rife with speculation that Japanese monetary authorities would tap the market with dollar bids as they have been clearly unhappy with the recent advance in the yen. However, traders noted that market conditions on Friday were not ideally suited for such a move. \par \par \uc2  "The market is long of dollars, thus it is not an ideal time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in," said Shuzo Kakuta, senior deputy general manager at Mizuho Corporate Bank. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by monetary authorities is most effective when short positions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are piled up in the market. Under such conditions, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could prompt short-covering, boosting upward momentum in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 123.20/30 compared with 123.29 yen in late New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at $0.9368/73 and 115.50/63 yen, compared with $0.9372 and 115.69 yen in late New York. \par \par \uc2  In New York on Thursday, the dollar slumped to fresh six-month lows against the yen at 122.82 and eased to near 16-month lows on the euro at $0.9415 amid continued losses in Wall Street stocks. \par \par \uc2  Concerns about the pace of the U.S. recovery and the U.S. current account deficit on top of the poor Wall Street performance have led the dollar to tumble nine percent versus the yen from this year's peak of 135.20 in late January. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the greenback has depreciated by 10 percent from this year's peak of $0.8560 in early February. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones industrial average closed down 0.11 percent at 9,911.69 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  EYED \par \par \uc2  Unlike U.S. and European officials, who have indicated little concern so far with the dollar's recent losses against the euro, the market believes Japanese officials are willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the U.S. Treasury said there had been no change in the administration's dollar policy as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped to new lows against the euro and the yen. \par \par \uc2  "There is no change in policy," said Michele Davis, a Treasury spokeswoman. U.S. Treasury officials have said in the past that they believe in a strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Top Japanese financial policymakers made various warnings against a further rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said that recent moves in the yen's exchange rate had been rapid, adding he had ordered ministry officials to closely monitor movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Authorities in Tokyo bought dollars for yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week after the dollar fell below 124 yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan fears a rapid rise in the yen could hurt an export-led recovery in its still fragile economy. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, said on Friday he saw no need for the yen to rise, adding that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remained unchanged. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has been undervalued, so it is natural for it to strengthen. But the situation is not the same for the yen. I don't think there is a need for the yen to rise," Kuroda said. Most in the market expect Moody's Investors Service to announce a one-notch downgrade to A1 from Aa3 in Japan's yen debt rating later in the day, but some anticipated an affirmation with a negative outlook. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of a two-notch cut have receded after Moody's upgraded Italy this month, but this is still seen possible. \par \par \uc2  Whatever the outcome, dealers said the announcement was unlikely to radically change the dollar's downward trend. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar was quoted at 1.5617/27 Swiss francs compared with 1.5600 francs in late New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In New York, the franc set a new 2-= year high against the dollar at 1.5550 francs as markets chose the traditional safe-haven Swiss franc with Mideast violence unabated and rising tensions between India and Pakistan. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0236 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 30 May.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9369   0.9367   +0.02    +5.22   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen               123.25   123.24   +0.01    -6.37   131.63\par  Euro/yen              115.53   115.53   +0.00    -1.46   117.24\par  Dlr/swiss             1.5615   1.5619   -0.03    -5.90   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr               1.4652   1.4653   -0.01    +0.76   1.4541\par  Can/dlr               1.5342   1.5338   +0.03    -3.61   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr               0.5661   0.5632   +0.51   +10.87   0.5106\par  Euro/swiss            1.4632   1.4633   -0.01    -1.00   1.4780\par  Euro/stg              0.6394   0.6390   +0.06    +4.43   0.6123.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020531dy5v005qd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
