\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Firm Vs Yen As Japan MOF Keeps Heat On \b0\par\par\uc2  By Audrey McAvoy \par \uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2002\par 07:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar was firm against the yen in Asian trade Tuesday as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players remained reluctant to sell the greenback and test Japanese authorities' resolve to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prevent the yen from rising. \par \par \uc2  Officials at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the market on its toes Tuesday by reminding it they are watching exchange rates and indicating that they are still ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "Given that the yen went from being weak to suddenly being strong, I don't think the market will stabilize," Masajuro Shiokawa told a regular press conference Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "More fluctuations are likely, but we will be carefully watching the movements of the market," he added. \par \par \uc2  Traders said these comments hinted the ministry might buy dollars at higher levels against the yen than it has in the past. \par \par \uc2  "That they would make these comments even with the dollar/yen where it is now raises the prospect they may come into the market above Y124," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  The levels at which the ministry has ordered the Bank of Japan to buy dollars has inched higher, he noted, from Y123.60/70 on the first occasion last week and then at just under Y124 on the second. \par \par \uc2  Satoshi Tate, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank, said speculative players are now reluctant to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below the Y124.50 mark. \par \par \uc2  The dollar should continue to trade between Y124.70 and Y125.25 during the remainder of global trade Tuesday, Tate said. \par \par \uc2  Sales orders from Japanese exporters needing to unload dollars before the end of the month capped the dollar at Y124.92 early, traders said. Its low in Asian trade was Y124.69. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y124.73, unchanged from late Monday in Toronto. The dollar was at Y124.79 late Monday in Tokyo. U.S. markets were closed Monday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9213, higher than $0.9204 late Monday in Toronto. The euro was at $0.9212 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y114.91, up from Y114.80 in Toronto late Monday. The euro was at Y114.96 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.4559, down from $1.4568 in Toronto but higher than $1.4566 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  But with the market still focused on the outlook for U.S. share prices and the U.S. economy, traders said they had little choice but to wait for U.S. markets to open after the long weekend and provide direction for the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Key U.S. data due later Tuesday, including Conference Board consumer confidence numbers for May at 1400 GMT, will be watched for hints on the U.S. economic outlook, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese finance ministry's aggressiveness to prevent the yen from strengthening may be in part designed to preempt a rise in reaction to what is likely to be strong Japanese gross domestic product data for the January to March quarter, said Koichi Udagawa, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at ABN Amro. \par \par \uc2  The consensus forecast of economists surveyed by Dow Jones and Nikkei News estimates GDP rose 1.6% from the previous quarter for a 6.7% annualized rate of increase. The government will release the data on June 7. \par \par \uc2  "The MOF is willing to protect the dollar/yen before the GDP announcement. The dollar is now weak, but there is a risk this could change to the yen being strong," Udagawa said. \par \par \uc2  Once the GDP numbers are issued, it will be more difficult for the ministry to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars, and it will likely have to allow the greenback to fall below Y123, he added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture, which is\par updated hourly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Subscribers can find this table:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020528dy5s0009v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
