\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Upbeat German Ifo survey buoys euro, market calm. \b0\par\par\uc2  By James Thornhill \par \uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2002\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 27 (Reuters) - The euro found support on Monday after a surprisingly strong German Ifo survey of business sentiment for May suggested the euro zone's largest economy is on the road to recovery. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the day's highs around $0.9220 after the headline West German sentiment index came in at 91.5, well above an analysts' consensus forecast of 90.6 and up from 90.5 in April. \par \par \uc2  However, the euro failed to build on an initial move higher following the release and markets were generally calm with a national holiday in the U.S. keeping trade thin. \par \par \uc2  "After the euro's initial run-up we've been slightly disappointed with the follow through...people are just belting themselves in for a very quiet day," said Kamal Sharma at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  Sharma said it was unlikely the euro would test last week's eight-month highs against the dollar around $0.9280, while the $0.9170/80 level was seen lending support. \par \par \uc2  By 0950 GMT the euro traded at $0.9207, up a touch from Friday's U.S. closing levels, and firmer against the yen at 114.99. \par \par \uc2  The economist in charge of the Ifo institute survey, Gernot Nerb, said the latest release showed that the German recovery is now in place, but added that the economy remained subdued with consumer demand still weak because of high unemployment. \par \par \uc2  Nerb also advised against a rate hike from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying the economy is still too weak and that there are no big inflation risks. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the yen was steady against the dollar as the positive impact from strong Japanese stocks was offset by wariness over possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  The yen traded at 124.87 to the dollar, little changed on the day. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  NERVES DOG YEN \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Nikkei average reached 12,081.43 on Monday, its highest since August 8, on hopes that a recovering economy would help banks write off huge bad loans. \par \par \uc2  But the yen could not capitalise on it, with dealers worried about the potential for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit its strength. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities, nervous that a strong yen could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-led recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday and Thursday to buy the greenback after the yen firmed to a 5-1/2 month high of 123.50 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "For the yen, wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still so strong and the dollar is holding onto gains made last week even with the gains in Nikkei," said David Mann, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities on Monday kept up their pressure against a strengthening yen, with senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi saying he was still monitoring the market. \par \par \uc2  Focus is now shifting on to the release of Japan's gross domestic product figures for the Japan-March quarter on June 7, which are widely expected to show growth of perhaps as much as eight or nine percent on an annualised basis. \par \par \uc2  "If the (Japanese GDP) figures are as good as many predict, another sell-yen factor will leave the market," said Kazuo Takayama, vice president at Toronto-Dominion Bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Ratings firm Moody's Investors Service is expected to announce some time this week the decision of its credit review of Japanese sovereign debt that it has been conducting since mid-February. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020527dy5r00jaq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
