\par\par \b \uc2  Yen fails to make gains due to wariness over BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2002\par 09:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 27 (Reuters) - The yen failed on Monday to draw strength from a bullish Tokyo share market, which rose to a fresh 2002 high, with concern over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities holding bulls back in quiet trade. Activity was dull throughout the day, with the dollar moving in a tight range of 124.70 to 124.96 yen. Many operators refrained from taking new positions due to market holidays in the United States and Singapore on Monday. \par \par \uc2  As of 0544 GMT, the dollar stood at 124.77/80 yen, little changed from the late U.S. level of 124.62/70. \par \par \uc2  "A downward revision in U.S. GDP growth and today's strength on the Nikkei could have been good dollar-selling factors, but the market refrained from selling because of nervousness over the Bank of Japan," a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at a securities firm said. \par \par \uc2  "It seems the market is extremely nervous about going short of dollars after last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the U.S. government revised its estimate of first-quarter gross domestic product (GDP) down to an annualised 5.6 percent from 5.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei average reached 12,081.23 in Monday morning trade, its highest since August 8, on hopes that a recovering economy would help banks write off huge bad loans. \par \par \uc2  As of 0544 GMT, the Nikkei was at 11,997.73. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities, nervous that a strong yen could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-led recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday and Thursday to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yen firmed to a five-and a-half-month high of 123.50 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also sluggish on Monday, with the euro at 92.07/13 cents against Friday's late New York level of 91.88 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at 114.89/5.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  The market is waiting for a series of euro zone data starting later on Monday with Germany's producer prices and Ifo business sentiment index at 0800 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Economists expect a slight improvement in the headline West German Ifo index to 90.6 in May from 90.5 in April. \par \par \uc2  Traders were also looking to pan-euro zone GDP data, as well as current account and inflation data from Italy, later in the week. \par \par \uc2  FOCUS MOVING TO JAPAN GDP \par \par \uc2  The market was shifting its focus to the release of Japan's gross domestic product figures for the Japan-March quarter on June 7, which are widely expected to show growth of perhaps as much as eight or nine percent on an annualised basis. \par \par \uc2  "If the (Japanese GDP) figures are as good as many predict, another sell-yen factor will leave the market," said Kazuo Takayama, vice president at Toronto-Dominion Bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "But given the limited dollar downside, I think the GDP will not have such a direct impact." \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities on Monday kept up their pressure against a strengthening yen, with senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi saying he was still monitoring the market. \par \par \uc2  "It's not good for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates to change rapidly. Stable moves are desired," Mizoguchi, head of the ministry's international bureau, told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Ratings firm Moody's Investors Service is expected to announce some time this week the decision of its credit review of Japanese sovereign debt that it has been conducting since mid-February. \par \par \uc2  Though Moody's has warned that the outcome could be a cut by up to two notches, traders showed little interest. \par \par \uc2  "It's pretty much forgotten. A downgrade has already been factored in," said a trader at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0600 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   24 May. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9208   0.9198   +0.11    -3.03   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen        124.78   124.71   +0.06    +9.03   114.45\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    114.84   114.82   +0.02    +5.64   108.71\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.5815   1.5831   -0.10    -1.23   1.6012\par  Stg/dlr        1.4572   1.4576   -0.03    -2.85   1.5000\par  Can/dlr        1.5337   1.5320   +0.11    +2.84   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr        0.5575   0.5565   +0.18    -0.34   0.5594\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss  1.4560   1.4571   -0.08    -4.34   1.5221\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg    0.6319   0.6312   +0.11    -0.09   0.6325\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ..  Debt... Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Official rates...\par \f28 \par \par \b \hi