\par\par \b \uc2  Philippine Peso Ends Dn;Dlr Above PHP50 1st Time In 3 Wks \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2002\par 10:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA -(Dow Jones)- The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed sharply lower Friday as the dollar broke above its key 50-peso resistance for the first time in three weeks on worries that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to weaken the yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at PHP50.35 on the Philippine Dealing System, its highest level since hitting PHP50.52 on May 2. It closed PHP49.840 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit an intraday high of PHP50.38 and averaged PHP50.090 compared with the previous session's PHP49.828. \par \par \uc2  Volume rose to $220.5 million from $187.5 million Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar's steady advance against the peso was spurred by the yen's losses. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened against the dollar on fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold yen twice this week. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan sold the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the Asian day Wednesday and after the Asian close Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar Friday rose to above Y125 from Y124.91 late Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Many are reluctant to short the dollar at this point because it may further strengthen," a local bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  Some traders believe the rising conflict between India and Pakistan added to the bearish sentiment on the peso, as a conflict may make investors shun developing markets for safe-haven investments, such as U.S. Treasurys. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buanaventura said the peso's decline was in line with the losses in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and shouldn't be a cause for worry. \par \par \uc2  Buanaventura said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso and is allowing market forces to determine its level. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said an easing of the tensions in India and Pakistan should allow the peso to strengthen to PHP49 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In the secondary market for Philippine treasury bills and bonds Friday, yields were flat, with banks reluctant to take fresh positions ahead of an early June announcement of May's inflation rate. \par \par \uc2  Some three-year bonds were dealt at 9.5%, unchanged from the previous level, while the three-month paper's yield was quoted at a stable 4.75%. \par \par \uc2  -By Ditas Lopez, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-885-0288; ditas.lopez@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1060 1853 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020524dy5o000hz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
