\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Lingering  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Lift Dlr Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Audrey McAvoy \par \uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2002\par 07:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar inched higher against both the yen and euro in Asian trade Friday as lingering fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities dissuaded players from selling the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  "There was some profit taking earlier, but then the dollar began rising as no one was selling it," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a major Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  "It was difficult to sell the dollar below Y124.00, where the authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , directed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sold yen for dollars on Thursday and Wednesday, halting a slide in the dollar that had been underway since last week. \par \par \uc2  Ministry officials said they took action as a rapid rise in the value of the yen is disruptive to the economy. \par \par \uc2  Players suspect the ministry will move to sell the yen again if the dollar falls towards Y124. \par \par \uc2  Still, there were elements to the dollar's moves Friday that had some convinced the dollar was not being propped up by fear alone. Though initially given a boost by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. unit has since rebounded on its own accord, they said. \par \par \uc2  "This correction is for real. The dollar has hit bottom against the yen," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Japanese brokerage, adding that the dollar may head back up over Y126 as its weakness is corrected over the next two to three weeks. \par \par \uc2  Demand for dollars from Japanese banks was unexpectedly strong in Tokyo trade Friday, which also helped the dollar rise, said a European bank trader. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y125.09, above Y124.91 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y124.31 late Thursday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9197, lower than $0.9215 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $0.9253 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y115.05, down from Y115.10 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y115.02 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.4534, down from $1.4540 in New York and lower than $1.4585 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's correction may also drag the euro down to $0.9100, especially if stop-loss sell orders at $0.9150 are triggered, the brokerage dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The euro may consolidate between 91 cents and 93 cents over the next month, he added. \par \par \uc2  In what may prove to be the initial stage of this consolidation, the euro fell below $0.9200 on Friday for the first time since May 16. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also stronger against the Swiss franc, rising to CHF1.5828 in late Asian trade from CHF1.5779 late Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at HSBC in Tokyo said Japanese authorities will need to do more to keep the dollar afloat, if only against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The bias is still downward. If there is no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it will drop off again," Ogino said. \par \par \uc2  Part of the problem is that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are still not certain whether the ministry has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  mainly to keep the dollar from sliding or if it plans to raise the greenback. \par \par \uc2  In the last series of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, Japanese authorities sold the yen repeatedly over several days and succeeded in raising the dollar's trading range against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that time began when the dollar was trading at Y116.85 and continued until the U.S. unit rose above Y120. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still trying to figure out if MOF is smoothing or intentionally lifting up the dollar," Ogino added. \par \par \uc2  -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture, which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020524dy5o0009s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
