\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar locked down by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  wariness. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2002\par 08:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 24 (Reuters) - Nervousness about the prospect of more Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept dollar/yen locked in a tight range near 125 yen in Asia on Friday as the market kept an eye on the 124 level, seen as trigger point for the BOJ's next move. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ sold yen for dollars on Wednesday and Thursday on concerns that the yen's rise to its highest levels in more than five months could derail Japan's tentative export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have also made it clear they will step into the market again if the yen rises too quickly. \par \par \uc2  "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is unchanged," Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa told a news conference. "We want \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates to be stable," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimate the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $3 billion in the latest round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and could do so again. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted around 125.05 yen at 0620 GMT, little changed from its late New York level. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ stepped into the market on Wednesday and Thursday when dollar/yen dropped to around 123.80/90. \par \par \uc2  The yen has risen more than six percent since the start of April, reflecting both concern about the quality of the U.S. recovery and signs \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy was finally bottoming out. \par \par \uc2  "The second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday gave us the impression that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned about the 124 yen level, rather than the speed of the dollar's fall," said a dealer at a European bank, repeating a widespread view in the market. \par \par \uc2  Trading was quiet. \par \par \uc2  "You can't sell the dollar because of concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  "On the other hand, Japanese exporters are ready to sell above 125 yen." \par \par \uc2  The market was slow ahead of the long Memorial Day weekend in the United States. There will be limited U.S. trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  FUND FLOWS \par \par \uc2  The yen has also been supported by browing expectations that investors would return to Japanese equities after having been significantly underweight for many months. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, there are renewed doubts about U.S. stocks, which have turned in a lacklustre performance recently despite signs of a moderate economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  While nervousness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is hampering a further advance by the yen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could gain momentum again if funds continue to flow into Japanese stocks, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "From last November to April, foreign investors sold 3.5 trillion yen ($28 billion) of Japanese securities," said Shinichi Sato, research manager at Tokyo-Mitsubishi Securities. \par \par \uc2  "If that much money is coming back, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will test the downside on the dollar again," he said. \par \par \uc2  A possible catalyst for an inflow of funds is Japan's January-March gross domestic product data due on June 7. \par \par \uc2  Economists' forecasts for annualised GDP growth range from six to even nine percent, exceeding the 5.8 percent recorded in the United States for the same period. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quiet. As of 0600 GMT it stood around 91.90/95 cents, little changed from 92.06 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, it stood at 114.97/01, compared with 115.20 yen. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0604 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 23 May.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9193   0.9206   -0.14    +3.25   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen               125.09   125.03   +0.05    -4.97   131.63\par  Euro/yen              115.02   115.20   -0.16    -1.89   117.24\par  Dlr/swiss             1.5823   1.5782   +0.26    -4.65   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr               1.4537   1.4549   -0.08    -0.03   1.4541\par  Can/dlr               1.5387   1.5356   +0.20    -3.33   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr               0.5540   0.5558   -0.32    +8.50   0.5106\par  Euro/swiss            1.4551   1.4537   +0.10    -1.55   1.4780\par  Euro/stg              0.6323   0.6327   -0.06    +3.27   0.6123.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020524dy5o00d9x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
