\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Ends Higher, Helped by Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry and Grainne McCarthy \par \uc2 862 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2002\par 23:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -- For the first time this week, the dollar made impressive inroads against the yen Thursday after a second day of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar also took back some ground from the euro and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although despite that broader rebound, many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts expect the greenback to resume its slippage fairly soon. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York Thursday, the dollar was trading around 124.91 yen, off its 125.32 yen session high, but nonetheless steady with levels reached after Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and much higher than 124.18 yen late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 92.15 U.S. cents, having retreated from its eight-month highs charted Wednesday, and down from 92.65 cents late Wednesday in New York. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at 1.5779 Swiss francs, up from 1.5697 francs late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.4540, down from $1.4605. \par \par \uc2  "I still think the general feeling is to sell dollars where possible," said John McCarthy, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Barings Capital Markets in New York, citing concerns about warnings of terrorist threats "that will be hanging over the dollar." \par \par \uc2  Following the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the European trading session, the greenback got a second wind early in New York from stronger-than-expected April durable-goods orders, up 1.1%. The U.S. unit broke above the key 125-yen mark as a result, hovering fairly close to that level towards the end of the session, as a late rally on U.S. equity markets gave the dollar some extra allure. \par \par \uc2  Unlike with some previous bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be reaping some immediate fruits of success now, partially because of the way in which the Bank of Japan flagged its actions to the markets and also because it is attempting to stabilize the yen rather than turn the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around, analysts reckon. \par \par \uc2  "Their goal was a modest one: to introduce double-sided risk into this market and they've achieved that," said Jim McCormick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers in New York. \par \par \uc2  After weeks of speculation, the Bank of Japan had showed its hand early in the Tokyo afternoon on Wednesday, buying up to $3 billion, with the second bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  coming after Tokyo markets had closed on Thursday, a factor that also arguably further increased the effectiveness of the action. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone in Tokyo was at the bar when they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jeremy Fand, a portfolio manager with Friedberg Mercantile Group in New York. "They are getting far more savvy," he added. \par \par \uc2  Underlying the initial success of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a sense that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't trying to target a specific exchange rate, but rather to smooth market movement. "If there is anything that the [\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] learned in the 1990s about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tactic, not a strategy," said David Gilmore, a partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Conn. "Setting objectives for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggests strategy. Smoothing is in keeping with tactics." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan does appear to have succeeded in shifting near-term trading ranges, with the dollar now expected to fluctuate somewhere between 124 yen -- around where Japanese authorities would be expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again -- and 125.40 yen, said Mr. McCarthy. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, some said that efforts to control the firming yen may be ultimately swept aside by a tide of dollar-negative market sentiment, as well as flows that play in Japan's favor based on the perception that the world's second biggest economy is at last gaining a modicum of momentum. "The problem you have is this isn't the classic risk-aversion yen-specific move a la post Sept. 11," said Mr. McCormick. "There's a fundamental story going on globally and the recovery has been very good for Asia, including Japan." \par \par \uc2  What's more, the Bank of Japan will start to lose its impact if it appears in the market too regularly. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  works best when it's unexpected and when it can successfully nudge a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the direction the market wants to take it in anyway. Now, the Bank of Japan has neither of those elements on its side. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, among the beneficiaries of geopolitical uncertainty, the price of gold once again jumped, edging ahead by more than $3 per ounce, to a fresh 23-month high at $321.50, as a slew of concerns persuaded worried investors to look for the safest place to park their funds. The precious metal is acting as a countervailing force to a weakening dollar, which may continue to be forced lower by disappointment about the U.S. economic recovery being less robust than expected, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But the South African rand -- viewed as a proxy for gold -- made only slight gains, with the dollar trading at 10.1500 rands late Thursday, down from 10.1655 rand Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2002 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020523dy5n00aca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
