\par\par \b \uc2  GLOBAL YIELD: BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fuels Bid For Treasurys \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry \par \uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2002\par 22:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- If \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to weaken the yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, U.S. Treasury bonds could be in for a considerable boost in the weeks ahead, global fixed-income strategists said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's purchases of dollars for yen this week on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  have already provided a modest boon to Treasurys, partly helping to push yields of shorter maturities lower. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , undertaken Wednesday and Thursday, have tallied a combined total of between $3.0 billion and $4.0 billion, said Ian Douglas, a global bond strategist with UBS Warburg in London. Other analysts speculate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have spent more. If other such \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  follow, they could become one factor "slowing a cyclical bearish move on the Treasurys market", Douglas said. \par \par \uc2  Over the past two sessions, traders ascribed part of the bid in short-dated Treasury notes to a perception among bond market participants that the Bank of Japan will need to use these maturities to park its newly-acquired dollars. \par \par \uc2  Japanese accounts in general have a track record of using Treasurys for this purpose and are among the biggest holders of U.S. government bonds. During past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as those undertaken after the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks, the BOJ has used part of its dollars to buy Treasurys, market analysts said. One key reason is the higher returns that U.S. fixed-income securities offer, with Japanese bond yields still scraping such low levels by comparison. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, tracing the original source of bids is tricky and based more on hearsay than proof at this point, fixed-income strategists said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  One reason why traders are a bit flummoxed about exactly how big a role the BOJ is playing in the bid for shorter Treasury maturities is that these securities are also tapping more of a flight-to-quality bid when U.S. equities show weakness and because of the ongoing concerns about terrorist threats. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Delayed Reaction\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Extrapolating the impact of such flows from Japan's official\par institutions can also prove tricky because there are several channels\par via which yen-denominated assets can be transformed into Treasury bonds.\par Either the BOJ can buy Treasurys directly in the market, or the money\par can flow indirectly via Japanese commercial banks, or through other\par global central banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In addition, the Federal Reserve acts as a custodian in accounts it\par maintains on behalf of foreign official institutions including central\par banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bulk of such transactions originating at the BOJ may have only\par just started to make themselves felt, however.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Expect a day or two's lag before the full weight of the BOJ's last two\par rounds of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit the Treasury market, says Tony\par Crescenzi, chief bond market analyst at Miller Tabak in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It is very likely" there will be more Treasurys purchases "either\par directly by the BOJ, or possibly via central banks in Europe," later\par Thursday, on Friday and on Tuesday after the long Memorial Day weekend\par in the U.S., Crescenzi said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Purchases of Treasurys "might have some exaggerated impact on Friday,\par amid lighter trading conditions," as U.S. bond markets wind up ahead of\par the long weekend, said John Canavan, market analyst with research\par company Stone & McCarthy in Princeton, N.J.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Watch For More BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite rebounding against the yen in the wake of Thursday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stronger-than-expected U.S. economic data, the dollar\par will soon come under pressure again, forcing more rounds of BOJ\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and more purchases of foreign assets, Canavan expects.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In September 2001 when the BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, buying\par around $23 billion before Sept 11, this resulted in "a massive spike in\par the buying of dollar bonds by Japanese investors" in October, UBS\par Warburg's Douglas wrote in a research note Thursday. This pattern could\par well be repeated over the next few weeks, he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Over the longer term, however, any near term gains the Treasurys\par market may make from such BOJ actions may be canceled out if later there\par are major portfolio outflows from U.S. assets amid a tide of\par prevailingly negative dollar-sentiment, warned Crescenzi.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By John Parry; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4083 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020523dy5n00c1e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
