\par\par \b \uc2  Focusing On Tactics, BOJ Reaps Some  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Success \b0\par\par\uc2  By Grainne McCarthy \par \uc2 956 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2002\par 21:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- It may be early days in terms of Japan's latest foray into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but analysts are already giving some kudos to the Bank of Japan for its part in stabilizing the rampaging yen by planting an element of doubt in a market that had been bent on pushing the yen stronger, even though many analysts are uncertain if the success will last. \par \par \uc2  "Their goal was a modest one: to introduce double-sided risk into this market and they've achieved that," said Jim McCormick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers in New York. \par \par \uc2  By far the most ardent practitioner of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  among the world's most powerful nations, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  - acting via its agent the BOJ - ended weeks of speculation on Wednesday by stepping into the market during Tokyo trade to buy dollars for yen. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed up during London trading on Thursday with similar purchases, in both instances helping to slow the pace of the yen's rise, a trend that had been in place for much of the past month. \par \par \uc2  Unlike with some previous bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be reaping some immediate fruits of success now, partially because of the way in which the BOJ flagged its actions to the markets and also because it is attempting to stabilize the yen rather than turn the entire direction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around, analysts reckon. \par \par \uc2  "They are getting far more savvy," said Jeremy Fand, a portfolio manager with Friedberg Mercantile Group in New York. He points, for instance, to the fact that the BOJ made a series of phone calls to major banks on Tuesday, effectively dropping a hefty hint that it was considering taking action. \par \par \uc2  According to several bankers who received the calls, the BOJ sought more information than it normally does as to why the yen was strengthening so much and in particular, whether the rally was being driven by speculative or longer-term investors. Presumably, the BOJ would already have known the answers to these questions, but in telephoning \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  desks at large banks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  created a sense that it might pull the trigger at any point. This message prompted investors to put on large amounts of short-dated dollar call options on Tuesday, in anticipation of some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Tokyo trading time. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  While They're In The Bar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sure enough, the BOJ showed its hand at around 2 p.m n Tokyo time  on\par Wednesday buying up to $3 billion, with the second bout of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par coming after Asian markets had closed on Thursday, a factor that also\par arguably further increased the effectiveness of the action. "Everyone in\par Tokyo was in the bar when they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Fand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Underlying the initial success of the action is a sense that unlike\par its usual form, Japan this time isn't trying to target an exchange rate,\par but to smooth market movements. "If there is anything that the (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) learned in the 1990's about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it is that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is a tactic, not a strategy," said David Gilmore,\par a partner at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Analytics in Essex, Conn. "Setting\par objectives for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suggests strategy. Smoothing is in keeping\par with tactics."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This message seems to have taken hold in the market,  injecting a\par reluctance on the part of traders to push the yen higher. Late in the\par New York day Thursday, the dollar was holding around Y124.91, off its\par Y125.32 session high, but nonetheless steady with levels reached after\par Thursday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Perhaps more tellingly, the dollar is up over\par 1% from seven-month lows  reached on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That's not to say that the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't start to strengthen\par in the weeks ahead, particularly if the BOJ starts to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  every\par day. Traditionally, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  works best when it's unexpected and\par when it can successfully nudge a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the direction the market\par wants to take it in anyway. Now, the BOJ has neither of those elements\par on its side, amid a sense that the cyclical recovery in Japan is bound\par to result in a stronger yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "You can't regain confidence in the Japanese economy, without having\par all Japanese asset prices rising," said Fand, referring to Japanese\par government bonds, stocks and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Perhaps mindful of this, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa has made\par it clear that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is specifically targeting the pace of the\par yen rally, rather than a particular line in the sand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market positioning has also been aiding the BOJ this time around.\par Unlike with the euro - where the short-term speculative community is\par running a massive long position - speculators are holding only a modest\par short dollar position against the yen. Traditionally, the BOJ is more\par reluctant to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the market action is dominated by speculators.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       Checkered History\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ has had somewhat of a checkered history with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par Last September, concerned that a strong yen might snuff out a nascent\par recovery in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly, buying\par dollars, as well as euro, for yen. Although, the bank lost the element\par of surprise by its regular appearances in the market, it did manage to\par ultimately push the dollar higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the period between January 1999 and April 2000 however, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into the market at least 18 times, including once via the\par Federal Reserve and European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But the market largely\par ignored the waves of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the yen continued to strengthen,\par hitting almost Y100 to the dollar by April 2000.\par     -Grainne McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2381;\par     Grainne.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020523dy5n00ane\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
