\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar moves up sharply as Japan sells yen again. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sumeet Desai \par \uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2002\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 23 (Reuters) - The dollar jumped nearly a yen within seconds on Thursday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for the second day running to curb the yen's export-damaging strength. \par \par \uc2  The greenback spiked from just around 123.90 to the day's high of 124.90 by 0934 GMT, less than a fifth of a yen below Wednesday's post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  high when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted after the dollar had hit a 5-1/2 month low. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had taken "appropriate action" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and that it was continuously acting in the market. \par \par \uc2  "It went absolutely barmy here. We reckon the Japanese were in at 123.90 and then bang, bang, here we go again. It just went flying," said Neil Parker, market strategist at RBS Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan bought dollars on Wednesday for the first time since September, concerned that the yen's recent appreciation could damage the country's nascent export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  The move lifted the $1-1/2 yen from five-month lows around 123.50 yen set earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan has the biggest reserves of any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the simple rule is don't bet against it," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of England declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ECB has in the past conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in European trading hours. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also retained a firmer footing against the euro, recovering almost half a cent from eight-month lows at $0.9280 plumbed on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Concerns over the strength of the U.S. recovery and the relative attraction of U.S. assets have weighed heavily on the dollar in recent weeks. Renewed fears of attacks on U.S. soil added to dollar bearishness this week. \par \par \uc2  GERMAN GDP \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed little reaction to news German economic growth sputtered back into life in the first three months of this year, reignited by a jump-start from exports. \par \par \uc2  Gross domestic product grew by 0.2 percent in the first quarter from the final quarter of 2001, when it contracted by 0.3 percent, the Federal Statistics Office said. \par \par \uc2  The pick-up in the first quarter, which followed two quarters of shrinking economic activity, came as little surprise after the Bundesbank this week estimated GDP rose around 0.25 percent in the first three months of this year. \par \par \uc2  The data beat analysts' forecasts for growth of 0.1 percent on the quarter. But economists warned that the foundations of the upturn were shaky, dependent largely on foreign demand rather than domestic consumer spending. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020523dy5n00j66\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
