\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar on hold as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worries persist. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2002\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 23 (Reuters) - The dollar managed to hold steady in Tokyo on Thursday, propped up by speculation that the Japanese authorities could step into the market to buy the greenback again following their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the dollar on Wednesday after it fell rapidly to a 5-= month low of 123.50 yen from around 128 in a few days on worries about the U.S. asset market and the latest concerns about terror attacks. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's move took many dealers by surprise, as they had assumed the BOJ would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when the dollar would fell below 120, and many players were not brave enough to sell the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "After watching the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers are scared to sell the dollar," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  "But on the other hand, you can't buy the dollar, simply counting on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  Thus the greenback was hovering around 124.30 yen in Tokyo, little changed from late New York levels and a touch above 123.80-123.90 levels where Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly rose as high as 125.10 yen shortly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it failed to maintain that level with Japanese exporters lined up to sell above 125 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Since the move to a strong yen was drastic, many exporters are still waiting to sell the dollar," said Masayuki Yamamoto, a research analyst at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment for the dollar has remained bearish on growing doubts about a speedy recovery in the U.S. economy and on optimism for the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  In another sign of confidence in Japan's economic recovery, foreign investors bought 359.2 billion yen of Japanese stocks last week, more than four times the 79.2 billion yen bought the previous week, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are now modifying portfolios that were very biased towards the U.S. On the other hand, most investors have been underweight Japanese stocks. Now they are moving Japanese stocks back to neutral," said Toshiyuki Aoyagi, manager at Nissho Iwai Corp. \par \par \uc2  SECURITY CONCERNS WEIGH \par \par \uc2  Nervousness over the prospect of more attacks in the United States also undermined U.S. stocks and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar sentiment has been bad from fears of possible terror attacks after U.S. Vice President (Dick) Cheney gave such a warning," a foreign bank dealer said. "Investors are worried that their dollar assets may be in danger." \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities kept up their warning against a stronger yen but there was no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday morning. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, the head of the Finance Ministry's international bureau, said they were still keeping a close watch on dollar-yen rates. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem yen's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "I think they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar falls below 124 yen. It's hard to think (a fall below) that level is OK today but wasn't OK yesterday," the Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, was quiet around 92.47 cents against Wednesday's Tokyo close of 92.42, off eight-month peak of 92.78 hit on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at 114.92 little moved from 114.95 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Some market players were waiting for the announcement of German first-quarter gross domestic product data by the government statistics office, which would give some clues on the strength of the recovery in the euro zone, and to the direction of the euro. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the Bundesbank said the economy grew 0.25 percent in the first three months of the year. Economists on average had forecast growth of 0.1 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0602 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   22 May. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9249   0.9256   -0.08    +3.87   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen        124.27   124.10   +0.14    -5.59   131.63\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    114.93   114.95   -0.02    -1.97   117.24\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.5710   1.5688   +0.14    -5.33   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr        1.4572   1.4587   -0.10    +0.21   1.4541\par  Can/dlr        1.5341   1.5318   +0.15    -3.62   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr        0.5568   0.5586   -0.32    +9.05   0.5106\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss  1.4532   1.4522   +0.07    -1.68   1.4780\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg    0.6344   0.6343   +0.02    +3.61   0.6123\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ..  Debt... Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \pa