\par\par \b \uc2  Swiss franc off highs as dollar finds support. \b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2002\par 08:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZURICH, May 23 (Reuters) - The Swiss franc was off its 28-month highs against the dollar in Europe on Thursday morning as the greenback found some support from talk of possible renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 1.5706/11 francs after falling to below 1.5660 on Wednesday. The euro traded at 1.4531/36 francs, which is also slightly higher than late levels of 1.4522 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders expected further action via the Bank of Japan as the yen remained strong after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss National Bank (SNB), however, is not expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to rein in the strong franc and economists said it was expected to continue its policy of reducing the money market repo rate by small steps. \par \par \uc2  UBS Warburg economists said the problem for the United States was that amid political and financial market uncertainty, the financing of its current account deficit was getting harder. \par \par \uc2  Also, for investments, the weaker dollar may become a self fulfiling prophecy for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks because investment ouflows in turn weaken the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Furthermore, Euroland seems to be better positioned to provide a higher return on investments than the U.S. as there are fewer signs of overinvestment," they said, adding they expected euro/dollar parity by the end of this year with dollar/franc at 1.50. \par \par \uc2  SNB CONDEMNED TO SIT BACK AND WATCH \par \par \uc2  The SNB is condemned to sit back and watch the franc rise against the dollar and the euro because any action to halt the franc's advances would be ineffective and could be counterproductive, economists said. \par \par \uc2  Janwillem Acket, chief economist at Julius Baer, said he expected the SNB to keep its rate cut ammunition dry until either the euro dropped below 1.40 to the franc or the benchmark three-month Swiss franc LIBOR rate was fixed below 1.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  The SNB, proud of its independence from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which gives the Alpine republic lower interest rates than those in euroland, lacks the size to move against the markets in the big pools of dollar and euro liquidity. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the SNB lowered its repo rate by two pips to 1.03 percent and it is expected to reduce this rate further step by step to curb the franc. \par \par \uc2  Later this week or early next, the rate set on the SNB's near-daily short-term money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  could fall below the pyschologically important level of 1.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Three-month LIBOR , the SNB's policy focus, eased to 1.24333 percent on Wednesday from 1.28167 percent on Tuesday, slipping just below the targeted midpoint of the 0.75-1.75 percent rate band used since a half-point cut on May 2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020523dy5n00b44\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
